.PP
The \fIUSED\fR column is \fBMemTotal\fR minus \fBMemAvailable\fR.
On kernels without \fBMemAvailable\fR, it falls back to total minus
free, buffers, and cache.
.PP
\fICACHE\fR includes \fBSReclaimable\fR (slab pages the kernel can
reclaim under memory pressure), in addition to the usual page cache.
Without this addition the \fICACHE\fR column would understate
reclaimable memory on systems with large dentry / inode caches.
.PP
Unit flags fall into two families:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-kilo\fR, \fB\-\-mega\fR, \fB\-\-giga\fR, \fB\-\-tera\fR,
\fB\-\-peta\fR use SI decimal units (powers of 1000).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-m\fR, \fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-tebi\fR, \fB\-\-pebi\fR use
binary units (powers of 1024).
.PP
With \fB\-h\fR (human-readable), \fB\-\-si\fR switches between the two.
.PP
Human-readable values use the first unit whose rounded one-decimal or
truncated integer representation fits three numeric columns. Thus
1000 KiB is displayed as \fB1.0Mi\fR, rather than \fB1000Ki\fR.
